---
title: Shop collection
layout: home
description: The things you sell. A shot, what it is, what it costs and one button — plus the two questions every buyer has before they press it, answered above the fold.
eyebrow: Collections · Shop
source: src/components/commerce.css
---
<section class="im-section im-wrap" style="padding-top: 1.5rem; --im-section-gap: 1.5rem">
	<p class="im-eyebrow">Collections · Shop · {{page.title}}</p>
	<p class="im-lede">{{page.description}}</p>
	<p class="doc-source"><code>{{page.source}}</code></p>
</section>

<div class="im-wrap-wide im-stack" style="--im-stack-gap: 2rem">
	<header class="im-collhead">
		<p class="im-eyebrow">Shop</p>
		<h1 class="im-collhead-title">Things I made, for sale</h1>
		<p class="im-collhead-text">Digital, delivered immediately, yours to keep. One licence covers every site you own — and everything here is what this site itself runs on.</p>
		<p class="im-collhead-meta"><span>{{demo.shop.length}} products</span><span>Instant download</span><a href="#shop">Licences</a></p>
	</header>

	<div class="im-collbar">
		<div class="im-collbar-filters">
			<a class="im-tag" href="#shop" aria-current="page">All</a>
			<a class="im-tag" href="#shop">Design systems</a>
			<a class="im-tag" href="#shop">Ghost themes</a>
			<a class="im-tag" href="#shop">Icons</a>
			<a class="im-tag" href="#shop">Free</a>
		</div>
		<div class="im-cluster" style="--im-cluster-gap: .375rem">
			<button class="im-btn im-btn-sm" type="button">{{icon "list-filter"}}Newest</button>
		</div>
	</div>

	<div class="im-repos" id="shop" style="--im-repos-min: 20rem">
		{{#each demo.shop}}
		<article class="im-product">
			<span class="im-product-media">
				<img src="{{lookup ../demo.shots @index}}" alt="" loading="lazy">
				{{#if badge}}<span class="im-kind im-kind-over" data-kind="issue">{{icon "sparkles"}}{{badge}}</span>{{/if}}
			</span>
			<p><span class="im-kind">{{icon "package"}}{{kind}}</span></p>
			<h3><a class="im-product-name" href="/collections/shop/product/">{{name}}</a></h3>
			<p class="im-product-text">{{text}}</p>
			<p class="im-product-foot">
				<span class="im-price{{#if free}} im-price-free{{/if}}">{{price}}{{#if was}}<span class="im-price-was">{{was}}</span>{{/if}}</span>
				<a class="im-btn im-btn-sm im-btn-primary" href="/collections/shop/product/">{{#if free}}Download{{else}}Buy{{/if}} {{icon "arrow-right"}}</a>
			</p>
		</article>
		{{/each}}
	</div>

	<section class="im-section">
		<div class="home-head"><p class="im-caption" data-index="q">Before you buy</p></div>
		<div class="im-grid-auto" style="--im-grid-min: 17rem">
			<div class="im-card im-card-outline"><span class="im-card-title">One licence, every site you own</span><span>Not per-site, not per-seat, not a subscription. Buy it once.</span></div>
			<div class="im-card im-card-outline"><span class="im-card-title">Updates for a year</span><span>And the version you have keeps working after that, forever.</span></div>
			<div class="im-card im-card-outline"><span class="im-card-title">Refunds, no argument</span><span>Fourteen days. You do not have to explain, and I will not ask.</span></div>
		</div>
	</section>
</div>

<section class="im-section im-wrap">
	<div class="im-prose">
		<h2>The card</h2>
		<p>A shot, what kind of thing it is, what it is called, one line, then the <strong>price and one button</strong> on the same row at the bottom. That row is what a shop card is for; everything above it is the argument for reading the row.</p>
		<div class="im-table-scroll">
		<table>
			<thead><tr><th>Class</th><th></th></tr></thead>
			<tbody>
				<tr><td><code>im-product</code></td><td>The card. It fills on hover, like every other card in the system.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>im-product-media</code></td><td>The shot, bled to the card's top edge. <code>--im-product-ratio</code>, 16:10.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>im-product-foot</code></td><td>Price on the left, button on the right, pushed to the bottom — so a row of cards with descriptions of different lengths still lines its prices up.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>im-price</code></td><td>Mono and tabular, because it is a number and a row of them should line up. <code>im-price-was</code> is what it used to be; <code>im-price-free</code> is the one that is not a number at all.</td></tr>
			</tbody>
		</table>
		</div>

		<h2>The three answers go above the fold</h2>
		<p>Every buyer of a digital product has the same three questions, and a shop that makes them hunt loses the sale: <strong>is it per-site</strong>, <strong>what happens when it updates</strong>, and <strong>can I get my money back</strong>. Answer them on the collection page, in three cards, before anybody has clicked into anything.</p>
		<p>It costs one row of the page and it is the difference between a shop and a list of files.</p>

		<h2>In a theme</h2>
		{{{{code "hbs"}}}}
{{#get "posts" filter="tag:#product" limit="all"}}
	<div class="im-repos" style="--im-repos-min: 20rem">
		{{#foreach posts}}
		<article class="im-product">
			<span class="im-product-media"><img src="{{img_url feature_image size="m"}}" alt=""></span>
			<h3><a class="im-product-name" href="{{url}}">{{title}}</a></h3>
			<p class="im-product-text">{{excerpt words="20"}}</p>
			<p class="im-product-foot">
				<span class="im-price">{{@custom.price}}</span>
				<a class="im-btn im-btn-sm im-btn-primary" href="{{url}}">{{t "Buy"}}</a>
			</p>
		</article>
		{{/foreach}}
	</div>
{{/get}}
		{{{{/code}}}}
		<p>Ghost has no product type, so a product is a post with an internal tag and the price in its code injection — or, if the shop is real, the price comes from whatever takes the payment, and the page never invents it.</p>
	</div>
</section>
